entity_ids.description:
Optional. The new IDs are the ones Home Assistant itself would give these entities today. History and statistics move along with them. {count} entities can get a shorter ID; {used} of them are used in your automations, scripts or dashboards.

Warning: an automation, script or dashboard that uses an old ID stops working until you change it. OpenThermostat's own dashboard follows by itself. You can undo this for {days} days. Other places, such as templates in YAML and other integrations, are not searched.

{preview}

e32_restore_confirm.description:
Backup of {created}, as the E32 checked it:

{summary}

The rooms keep the mode of the backup. The takeover of the boiler is not part of a backup: a new or reset E32 sends nothing to the boiler until you confirm the takeover on its page (Rooms → Active control). Before the restore Home Assistant also saves a backup of the E32 as it is now.

comfort_care.description:
{saved}The E32 sets these itself and keeps adjusting them as it learns your house. Change one only if you want it differently. The same settings as on the E32's Home page.

Now:
{settings}

ble_sensors.description:
{saved}The Bluetooth sensors paired with the E32. Rename or forget them here; collect all changes first and save them together: after saving, the E32 restarts once, about 30 seconds later, to use them. Pairing a new sensor (scan and key) is done on the E32's page System → Devices, next to the sensor. Which room a sensor measures is set per room under Rooms.

{sensors}

{pending}

ble_forget.description:
A forgotten sensor is no longer read by the E32; its key is deleted on the E32. To use it again, pair it again on the E32. A room that measures with it uses its other sources.

Sensors used by a room:
{used}

shelly_devices.description:
{saved}The Plug of the floor pump, The Pill with its temperature probes and the BLU Gateway of the radiator valves. The E32 talks to them itself over your home network, also without Home Assistant.

{devices}

The probe roles of The Pill, looking for valves at the gateway, and a device's name, address or password are set on the E32's page System → Devices.

shelly_valve_remove.description:
The E32 stops reading and driving these valves. A valve in a room stays there until you remove it under Rooms → the room → Radiator valves.

In a room now:
{rooms}

house_holidays.description:
{saved}Choose the house mode, or plan holidays ahead. On holiday every room stays at most the temperature on holiday and the house is warm again when you are back; then the house mode is as before.

Planned holidays:
{holidays}

boiler_settings.description:
{saved}The boiler's own settings, such as the hot water temperature. The boiler keeps them in its own memory. The E32 changes one only when you allow it, one at a time, and reads it back from the boiler. A setting not yet verified on your boiler is tried while you watch the boiler, and put back by itself unless you keep it.

Changing boiler settings: {state}

{settings}

notifications.description:
{saved}Messages on your phone. About a room (a window open while the room heats, a room that stays cold, a sensor or battery that needs attention): to the people chosen for that room on its screen on the Settings tab, or everyone with a phone until you choose. About the house (problems and maintenance of the boiler and the E32): only to the people with the tick "Also messages about the house". Nothing is on until you switch it on.

On now: {on}

Phones:
{people}

abort.e32_restore_done_online:
Settings restored. The E32 restarted and answers again. The rooms keep the mode of the backup; a new or reset E32 controls the boiler only after you confirm the takeover on its Rooms page.

Enter these again on the E32 page:
{reenter}

abort.e32_restore_done_waiting:
Settings restored. The E32 is restarting and did not answer yet; Home Assistant reconnects by itself as soon as it is back. The rooms keep the mode of the backup; a new or reset E32 controls the boiler only after you confirm the takeover on its Rooms page.

Enter these again on the E32 page:
{reenter}

abort.e32_restore_done_restart:
Settings restored. Restart the E32 (System → Restart device on its page) to use all of them. The rooms keep the mode of the backup; a new or reset E32 controls the boiler only after you confirm the takeover on its Rooms page.

Enter these again on the E32 page:
{reenter}

abort.e32_restore_done:
Settings restored. The rooms keep the mode of the backup; a new or reset E32 controls the boiler only after you confirm the takeover on its Rooms page.

Enter these again on the E32 page:
{reenter}

